    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "NLl6E",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note DS",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "DESIGN SYSTEM — tokens live as document variables (colors / spacing / radius / fonts); every screen is assembled from these reusable components via instances. Edit a component once, every instance updates. No external .pen imports: file must stay self-contained so the repo's headless CLI workflow can load it (the previous prototype broke on pencil:shadcn.lib.pen refs)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "zS7pG",
      "x": 1600,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S1",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S1 OVERVIEW · daemon up — #578 acceptance row 1. One glance answers did-it-run: three liveness proofs (pid / sock / rpc) shown separately, never folded into one boolean (#359 lesson); per-chain live runs + last transition; rateLimit cooldown; recent anomaly events. Data: status snapshot (SQLite ro) + events via SSE (#577)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "rtQSF",
      "x": 3200,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S2",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S2 OVERVIEW · daemon down — the RFC's founding scenario (#544 A-ruling, #578 row 2). Gateway outlives the daemon: death time, cause events (daemon.fatal), terminated runs, queue terminal state stay readable; one-click Start spawns `coder-loop daemon up`. Gateway still answering = daemon-down, not network-down."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "D4ECg",
      "x": 4800,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S3",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S3 CHAIN DETAIL — the tree IS the queue (#546: chain = top-level seq; flat item queue is a retired v2 projection). Node vocab from #546/#558: leaf/seq/par · join ADT drain | validator (+ reserved best-of-n | script) · seq cursor · reopen count/budget · par container stable id (= #545 group scope key). Gate hold lives on a decision point — here container.advance of par-a7f3, held by validator #618; unified contract advance | hold | reopen(target, corrections). Reorder grips + unblock act directly on tree leaves (#579 F-set). Hooks: observer points = event types, gate points = #543 closed set."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "JHPXk",
      "x": 6400,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S4",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S4 ITEM & ATTEMPT — #546: item = one preset call, expanding into the preset's phase task tree (rendered with seq cursor); every run gets its own worktree (per-run axiom, slot retired). #581 prompt view: prompt.md verbatim (same value argv got, #572 single-source), bindings.json KEY-to-value, FRESH/RESUME badges + resumed session, honest no-snapshot state for attempts predating #572."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Rzt7S",
      "x": 8000,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S5",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S5 EVENTS — #577 SSE live tail (fs.watch + offset, incremental, survives daemon death) with filters exactly on the envelope keys (chain / item / runId / phase / time / 5 kinds). Selected event shows raw JSONL envelope + jump-to-run / jump-to-item (#580 event-object cross links)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "i78tb9",
      "x": 9600,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note S6",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "S6 PRESET PREVIEW — #582/#549 compile artifact (schemaVersion-strict, six blocks: preset / statuses+stateGraph / phases+task tree / tools / fragments / findings). Phase tree renders the v3 target shape seq(analyze, par(implement, test), review) — goal 4's 'iter is three stages, two parallel'; today's gh-issue preset compiles to a degenerate seq (tree declaration lands with #554). Tools block: [[tools]] registry + per-phase toolRequirements, required|expected — required legal only for engine-kind tools. State graph: nodes = statuses, edges = which phase exit writes them + engine transitions entry/exhausted/unblock."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "m4EYq9",
      "x": 11200,
      "y": -210,
      "name": "Note Mobile",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "M1/M2 MOBILE (PWA) — #584: above-the-fold answers did-it-run (three proofs + anomalies + actions), no scrolling needed; deep views share the same routes as PC (no forked implementation). M2 = the F-ruling unblock / reorder / chain stop-resume acted from a phone."
    }
  ],
